What:		/dev/gvdu
Date:		August 2025
Contact:	Kanstantsin Yarmash <kyarmash@google.com>
Description:
		The /dev/gvdu device is a write-only character device for
		submitting a Volatile Debug Unlock (VDU) directive to the driver.

		Writing to this device buffers the directive within the driver. The
		directive will be processed upon release of the character device,
		which consumes the buffered data.

		The character device is protected by a single-open mechanism.

		The device accepts a single binary payload in the following format:

		Data:   | grant length | grant data | delegate length | delegate data |
		Format: |   uint32_t   |   base64   |    uint32_t     |    base64     |

		Where:
		 - grant length: A 32-bit unsigned integer in little-endian
		   format specifying the length of the 'grant data' string.

		 - grant data: The Base64-encoded grant string.

		 - delegate length: A 32-bit unsigned integer in little-endian
		   format specifying the length of the 'delegate data' string.

		 - delegate data: The Base64-encoded delegate string.
